const existingRecord = await prisma.webhookIdempotencyKey.findUnique({
  where: { idempotencyKey: event.request.idempotency_key }
});
if (existingRecord) return existingRecord.responseBody;


3. **Store the result** after processing, before returning to Stripe.

Why not Redux/in-memory cache? Because Metric Flow runs on Vercel (serverless), and you can't guarantee the same instance handles retries.

What does your current `createSubscriptionTransaction` function signature look like?

Check **before**. If you check after acquiring a lock, you're defeating the purpose—you'd still execute the side effects twice (or multiple times) before realizing you already did this work.

