Exactly—you've made the right architectural choice with gRPC streaming over polling, but the dependency graph is incomplete. The missing cleanup is a classic subscription management anti-pattern. The fix is straightforward: return a cleanup function that calls `subscription.cancel()` or `subscription.end()` (depending on your gRPC client library version). Also, I notice you don't have `subscription` in the dependency array, which means if the gRPC client changes, you won't re-establish the stream. Here's the corrected pattern:

